# ethren (M2.11): our character animations (tools/sprite_render writes the rows; the test games merge
# them into the demo's table). The engine uses the row with the largest id not above the CRE's, so each
# body owns a block of 16 ids (variants, outfits) and each species and gender a block of 0x10 bodies:
#   0x6500 human male    0x6510 human female   0x6520 dwarf male      0x6530 dwarf female
#   0x6540 elf male      0x6550 elf female     0x6560 halfling male   0x6570 halfling female
# 0x6500 CPM1 the male peasant, hair and beard baked in; 0x6501 CPM2 the same body bald and beardless,
# for the hair and beard overlays (dcchair.2da); 0x6510 CPF1 the female peasant (her hair baked in); 0x6511
# CPF2 the female body bald, for her hair layers (S4). TYPE 0 (IE_ANI_CODE_MIRROR),
# SPACE 2, PALETTE 0 (recoloured from the CRE's colours). SIZE is the overlays' letter (WQ<size><code>):
# weapons, helmets and hair are rendered on one rig, so each body has its own (L the male, F the female).
# S6: the demihumans' bald bodies, hair and beards always overlays: 0x6520 CDM2 the dwarf man (D), 0x6530 CDF2
# the dwarf woman (W), 0x6540 CEM2 the elf man (E), 0x6550 CEF2 the elf woman (V), 0x6560 CLM2 the halfling man
# (H), 0x6570 CLF2 the halfling woman (N).
